{"kind":"request","text":"Archive A2 and A3, to the fixture-only cutoff milestone of plan 032 (notes/plans/032-2026-10-17-journey-as-acceptance-target.md, section 2a; slice table at notes/2026-10-09-shared-language-volatile-acts.md:1833-1834; owed work at notes/implementation/2026-10-17-archive-layout.md:349-357). Next in the order after the card kit (6098b756): start when the card kit head is in checker review, before J3 (c097372e) and the evidence-rules slice (a53e1464).\n\nA2, Git source: gitSource, the --git, --texts and --receipt options, and the untrusted resolution of section 15.7. Witnesses as the table lists: one fixture history replayed from HTTP and from a clone gives the same report apart from trusts; four histories replay in replay mode from the clone alone, with no service and no anchor, each a pass whose cutoff ends at the entry that first needs the dependency (a declared genesis; an outcome that first introduces a value named by its evidence; an outcome that first names a snapshot of staged refs with no later act, reported incomplete and not missing-input; an observing delivery that first requires a retained value); a changed line, a cut segment and a wrong head.json are each mismatch; a missing foreign ref is missing-dependency; a clone with a symlink, a submodule or an out-of-grammar path under journal/v1/ is refused without touching the filesystem; a receipt is confirmed from the clone at its own position after the clone's integrity and continuity are checked, or reported mismatch or behind.\n\nA3, archiver: target resolution, the manifest and the bookkeeping row, the provider's archive token, send and read-back, on real object storage with a scripted host. Witnesses: a lost reply resolves by read-back with no second commit; a reset after Mark and before any object reached the host, then a turn that retains a new input, then a restart rebuilds the original commit byte for byte, reading only the dependencies the row names (the store instrumented to